          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 0,
              "bbox": [
                0.312,
                0.571,
                0.376,
                0.619
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_0.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the sum of two given angles is less than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 0 ^ { \\circ } ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , a triangle exists with these angles. If the sum is greater than or equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , there is no triangle with these angles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.143,
            0.845,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us take two angles, say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 0 ^ { \\circ } ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , whose sum is less than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let the included side be 5 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.19,
            0.848,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? What could the measure of the third angle be? Does this measure change if the base length is changed to some other value, say 7 cm? Construct and find out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.267,
            0.848,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ In general, once the two angles are fixed, does the third angle depend on the included sidelength? Try with different pairs of angles and lengths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.336,
            0.849,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The measurements might show that the sidelength has no effect (or a very small effect) on the third angle. With this observation, let us see if we can find the third angle without carrying out the construction and measurement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.418,
            0.803,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Try experimenting with different triangles to see if there is a relation between any two angles and the third one. To find this relation, what data will you keep track of and how will you organise the data you collect?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.422,
            0.905,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.818,
                0.422,
                0.905,
                0.475
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.515,
            0.847,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Consider a triangle ABC with "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle B = 50^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle C = 70^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Let us see how we can find "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " without construction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.398,
            0.557,
            0.597,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.398,
                0.557,
                0.597,
                0.681
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.688,
            0.847,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We saw that the notion of parallel lines was useful to determine that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.707,
            0.582,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the sum of any two angles of a triangle is less than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 0 ^ { \\circ } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Parallel lines can be used to find the third angle, ∠BAC as well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.762,
            0.582,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us suppose we construct a line XY parallel to BC through vertex A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.808,
            0.581,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can see new angles being formed here: ∠XAB, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathtt { Y A C } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What are their values?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.598,
            0.711,
            0.842,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.598,
                0.711,
                0.842,
                0.845
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_15.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.857,
            0.511,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since the line XY is parallel to BC,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.876,
            0.847,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{XAB} = \\angle \\mathrm{B}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{YAC} = \\angle \\mathrm{C},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , because they are alternate angles of the transversals AB and AC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.938,
            0.194,
            0.954
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "164"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
